    "audio": "Decode source audio to signed 16-bit, 16 kHz mono PCM using FFmpeg 7.1.5 as needed. The 60 MINDS-14 source recordings are mono 8 kHz G.711 µ-law WAV. Resampling did not change their durations or truncate them; the longest was 24.576 seconds.",
    "scoring": "Score raw output before the call rejects unknown results. Use Levenshtein edits divided by normalized reference units. For Mandarin CER the units are Unicode letters and numbers, counted as individual characters. In English WER each ASCII alphanumeric word is one unit and internal apostrophes stay in the word. In mixed error rate (MER), each Han character and each English word are one unit. Lowercase and fold curly apostrophes to straight apostrophes. Treat a literal <unk> as an unknown unit. An exact match has no edits. In mixed results, script counts say whether both Han and English tokens occur, independently of correctness.",
    "limits": "These deterministic samples are a subset of their corpora. Benchmarks use the public references as provided. Training overlap is unknown. More than half the reference words in the US telephone subset come from clips longer than eight seconds, and this subset had the highest English error rate. Mixed utterances remain harder than clear read speech."
